diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 835cfa34c2..b4f752704c 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -34,6 +34,9 @@ All notable, unreleased changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 
 ### GraphQL API
 
+- Added age restriction for products. `Product.minimumAge` (set with `ProductInput.minimumAge`) defines the minimum age in years a customer must have to buy the product, and `User.birthday` (set with `CustomerInput.birthday` and `AccountInput.birthday`) stores the customer's birthday. `checkoutCreate`, `checkoutLinesAdd`, `checkoutComplete` and `orderCreateFromCheckout` reject age-restricted products with the new `PRODUCT_AGE_RESTRICTED` and `BIRTHDAY_REQUIRED` error codes when the customer is too young, is a guest or has no birthday.
+- `User.birthday` is now visible only to the user themselves and to superusers. Changes to a birthday and reads of it by a superuser are recorded as the new `BIRTHDAY_CHANGED` and `BIRTHDAY_READ` customer events (`CustomerEventsEnum`). The events record who acted and which account, never the birthday itself.
+- The age used for age-restricted products, and the "birthday is not in the future" check, now use the current date in the shop's time zone instead of the UTC date. Set the new `SHOP_TIME_ZONE` environment variable to an IANA time zone name (for example `Europe/Warsaw`) to configure it; the default is `UTC`, and an invalid name stops the server from starting.
 - Added `deprecationReason` field to the `App` and `Manifest` types, and a new `appSelfUpdate` mutation that lets an app set it on itself. An app declares it in its manifest (`deprecationReason`) and/or sets it at any time via `appSelfUpdate`; staff users cannot set it through `appUpdate`. Pass a blank value to `appSelfUpdate` to clear it; omitting the field or passing `null` leaves it unchanged. Values longer than 2048 characters are truncated rather than rejected. A deprecated app keeps working exactly as before - the field is informational and is surfaced in the dashboard.
 - Added `identifier` field to the `Webhook` type. It holds an app-provided, stable identifier that is unique per app. It can be set through the app manifest (`webhooks[].identifier`) and the `webhookCreate`/`webhookUpdate` mutations.
 - Added `Shop.allowStorefrontTraffic` field and `ShopSettingsInput.allowStorefrontTraffic` input. When disabled, only apps and staff users may call the GraphQL API directly; anonymous requests and non-staff customers are rejected with HTTP 401 and the `STOREFRONT_TRAFFIC_NOT_ALLOWED` error code.
